What is SRE?

SRE (Site Reliability Engineering) is a discipline that combines software engineering and IT operations to ensure scalable, reliable, and high-performing systems. It was pioneered by Google to manage large-scale systems efficiently.

📌 SRE Key Responsibilities:

Monitoring & Alerting
Incident Response & Root Cause Analysis
System Performance & Reliability
Automation of Manual Operations
Capacity Planning & Load Management
Error Budget Management

🛠️ SRE Common Tools:

Prometheus / Grafana – Monitoring & dashboards
Alertmanager / PagerDuty / Opsgenie – Alerts & incident response
Terraform / Ansible / Chef – Infrastructure automation
Kubernetes / Docker – Container orchestration
Elasticsearch / Kibana / Splunk – Log analysis

